<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Remove Duplicate Triangles</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Remove &gt; Duplicate Triangles</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Remove Duplicate Triangles</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command finds any visible selected triangles that have identical vertices in the mesh and removes the surplus triangles even if the directions of their normals are opposite. It is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. This command works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB">Duplicated triangles could be generated when merge scan to mesh, when weld a mesh, or when import meshes from other CAD applications (see</span> <span class="Command">Open</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command description for details.) This is why it is useful after such operations to apply</span> <span class="Command">Remove Duplicate Triangles</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to the whole mesh.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','Remove Faulty Areas','remove_faulty_areas.htm','Remove Floating Meshes','remove_floating_meshes.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../add_on/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></p>
